{
  "slug": "obsidian-sync",
  "name": "Obsidian Sync",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A Claude Code plugin that syncs project documentation to your Obsidian vault — one command, zero config.\n\nThe Problem:\nYou clone repos. Each has scattered documentation — .md files, .pdf references — buried in nested directories. You want to read and search them in one place, but they live across dozens of project folders.\n\nobsidian-sync moves all project documentation into your Obsidian vault with a single command, keeping them browsable both in Obsidian and in the original project.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `obsidian-sync` (Sync project documentation files (.md, .pdf) to an Obsidian vault for unified knowledge management) and **1 command**, `obsidian-sync` (Sync project documentation (.md, .pdf) to Obsidian vault).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install obsidian-sync@claude-community` from `chenlei1700/obsidian-sync`.",
